---@class aws.route_53.HealthCheck
---@field Id aws.route_53.HealthCheckId The identifier that Amazon Route 53 assigned to the health check when you created it. When you add or update a resource record set, you use this value to specify which health check to use. The value can be up to 64 characters long.
---@field CallerReference aws.route_53.HealthCheckNonce A unique string that you specified when you created the health check.
---@field LinkedService? aws.route_53.LinkedService If the health check was created by another service, the service that created the health check. When a health check is created by another service, you can't edit or delete it using Amazon Route 53.
---@field HealthCheckConfig aws.route_53.HealthCheckConfig A complex type that contains detailed information about one health check.
---@field HealthCheckVersion aws.route_53.HealthCheckVersion The version of the health check. You can optionally pass this value in a call to UpdateHealthCheck to prevent overwriting another change to the health check.
