---A key-signing key (KSK) is a complex type that represents a public/private key pair. The private key is used to generate a digital signature for the zone signing key (ZSK). The public key is stored in the DNS and is used to authenticate the ZSK. A KSK is always associated with a hosted zone; it cannot exist by itself.
---@class aws.route_53.KeySigningKey
---@field Name? aws.route_53.SigningKeyName A string used to identify a key-signing key (KSK). Name can include numbers, letters, and underscores (_). Name must be unique for each key-signing key in the same hosted zone.
---@field KmsArn? aws.route_53.SigningKeyString The Amazon resource name (ARN) used to identify the customer managed key in Key Management Service (KMS). The KmsArn must be unique for each key-signing key (KSK) in a single hosted zone.
---@field Flag aws.route_53.SigningKeyInteger An integer that specifies how the key is used. For key-signing key (KSK), this value is always 257.
---@field SigningAlgorithmMnemonic? aws.route_53.SigningKeyString A string used to represent the signing algorithm. This value must follow the guidelines provided by RFC-8624 Section 3.1.
---@field SigningAlgorithmType aws.route_53.SigningKeyInteger An integer used to represent the signing algorithm. This value must follow the guidelines provided by RFC-8624 Section 3.1.
---@field DigestAlgorithmMnemonic? aws.route_53.SigningKeyString A string used to represent the delegation signer digest algorithm. This value must follow the guidelines provided by RFC-8624 Section 3.3.
---@field DigestAlgorithmType aws.route_53.SigningKeyInteger An integer used to represent the delegation signer digest algorithm. This value must follow the guidelines provided by RFC-8624 Section 3.3.
---@field KeyTag aws.route_53.SigningKeyTag An integer used to identify the DNSSEC record for the domain name. The process used to calculate the value is described in RFC-4034 Appendix B.
---@field DigestValue? aws.route_53.SigningKeyString A cryptographic digest of a DNSKEY resource record (RR). DNSKEY records are used to publish the public key that resolvers can use to verify DNSSEC signatures that are used to secure certain kinds of information provided by the DNS system.
---@field PublicKey? aws.route_53.SigningKeyString The public key, represented as a Base64 encoding, as required by RFC-4034 Page 5.
---@field DSRecord? aws.route_53.SigningKeyString A string that represents a delegation signer (DS) record.
---@field DNSKEYRecord? aws.route_53.SigningKeyString A string that represents a DNSKEY record.
---@field Status? aws.route_53.SigningKeyStatus A string that represents the current key-signing key (KSK) status.
---@field StatusMessage? aws.route_53.SigningKeyStatusMessage The status message provided for the following key-signing key (KSK) statuses: ACTION_NEEDED or INTERNAL_FAILURE. The status message includes information about what the problem might be and steps that you can take to correct the issue.
---@field CreatedDate? aws.route_53.TimeStamp The date when the key-signing key (KSK) was created.
---@field LastModifiedDate? aws.route_53.TimeStamp The last time that the key-signing key (KSK) was changed.

---@alias aws.route_53.KeySigningKeys aws.route_53.KeySigningKey[]

---@alias aws.route_53.Latitude string

---@alias aws.route_53.LimitValue number

